## Slide 6

Manually Splitting and Acknowledging Events

Events

In some cases, the automation may not record the desired pattern or split of Events. The more detailed and complex the configuration is, the higher the likelihood that some data becomes over tuned or missed entirely. If the Event is not attributed to the proper root cause by TrakSYS automation, it can be manually re-assigned through manual Acknowledgement processes.

In the example above, the Jam Event Definition took the entire duration of the downtime, but operations wants to reflect it as two different root causes. The original Event can be split into two root causes with the total duration split between the two. In manual assignment, the Sub-Events can be used to help with assigning proper root causes, but they do not limit operations from making the desired corrections.

Jam (Priority 1)
10 Minutes
Misfeed (Priority 2)
25 Minutes
E-Stop
15 Minutes
Low Temperature
20 Minutes

Desired Event
Jam Event - 15 Minutes
Misfeed Event - 20 Minutes
Original Event
Jam Event - 35 Minutes

